An allocation of a process takes none for its region slots,
and makes a process no region can ever be installed in.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: process has no region slot, or more than the hardware has entries
Witness: fuzz pool-runs-out

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -385,7 +385,7 @@ static int op_pool(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         }
         /* A region slot for each region it may have installed at once, one at least and an entry each at most. */
         uint32_t regions = arg[4];
-        if (regions == 0 || regions > pmp_entry_count) {
+        if (regions > pmp_entry_count) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         struct process *proc = pool_alloc(pool, CAP_PROCESS, obj_type_size(CAP_PROCESS, regions));
